last message posted as the comment, footer attached.

**A session-ending tool.** `create_pr`, `launch_sub_agent`,
`request_close_issue` and `reload_environment` end the session while they do
their work, and the comment they already wrote is the ending: the footer is
appended onto it, so the run still has exactly one.

A run that has nothing to say — it started on a comment that asked for nothing
new, say — ends without posting, and that is an ending too: the guard reads the
thread, not the absence of one. [What starts a run](what-starts-a-run.md) names
